INSERT INTO sections (id, test_id, type, title, instructions, audio_url, passage_text, order_index) VALUES
(1713, 171, 'reading', 'Reading Passage 3: To catch a king', '<div class="ielts-reading-container"><h2 class="ielts-reading-question-section-heading">
                                            Questions 27-31                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                    </h2>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-question-section-content">
                                            <div class="ielts-reading-section-content-wrapper"><p><em>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, <strong>A-J</strong>, below.</em></p>
<p class="ielts-reading-passage-subhead"><strong><strong>The story behind the hunt for Charles II</strong></strong></p>
<p>Charles II’s father was executed by the Parliamentarian forces in 1649. Charles II then formed a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">27</strong><select data-qnum="27" name="question_27" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 27 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. military innovation">A. military innovation</option><option value="B. large reward">B. large reward</option><option value="C. widespread conspiracy">C. widespread conspiracy</option><option value="D. relative safety">D. relative safety</option><option value="E. new government">E. new government</option><option value="F. decisive victory">F. decisive victory</option><option value="G. political debate">G. political debate</option><option value="H. strategic alliance">H. strategic alliance</option><option value="I. popular solution">I. popular solution</option><option value="J. religious conviction">J. religious conviction</option></select></span></span> with the Scots, and in order to become King of Scots, he abandoned an important <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">28</strong><select data-qnum="28" name="question_28" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 28 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. military innovation">A. military innovation</option><option value="B. large reward">B. large reward</option><option value="C. widespread conspiracy">C. widespread conspiracy</option><option value="D. relative safety">D. relative safety</option><option value="E. new government">E. new government</option><option value="F. decisive victory">F. decisive victory</option><option value="G. political debate">G. political debate</option><option value="H. strategic alliance">H. strategic alliance</option><option value="I. popular solution">I. popular solution</option><option value="J. religious conviction">J. religious conviction</option></select></span></span> that was held by his father and had contributed to his father’s death. The opposing sides then met outside Worcester in 1651. The battle led to a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">29</strong><select data-qnum="29" name="question_29" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 29 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. military innovation">A. military innovation</option><option value="B. large reward">B. large reward</option><option value="C. widespread conspiracy">C. widespread conspiracy</option><option value="D. relative safety">D. relative safety</option><option value="E. new government">E. new government</option><option value="F. decisive victory">F. decisive victory</option><option value="G. political debate">G. political debate</option><option value="H. strategic alliance">H. strategic alliance</option><option value="I. popular solution">I. popular solution</option><option value="J. religious conviction">J. religious conviction</option></select></span></span> for the Parliamentarians and Charles had to flee for his life. A <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">30</strong><select data-qnum="30" name="question_30" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 30 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. military innovation">A. military innovation</option><option value="B. large reward">B. large reward</option><option value="C. widespread conspiracy">C. widespread conspiracy</option><option value="D. relative safety">D. relative safety</option><option value="E. new government">E. new government</option><option value="F. decisive victory">F. decisive victory</option><option value="G. political debate">G. political debate</option><option value="H. strategic alliance">H. strategic alliance</option><option value="I. popular solution">I. popular solution</option><option value="J. religious conviction">J. religious conviction</option></select></span></span> was offered for Charles’s capture, but after six weeks spent in hiding, he eventually managed to reach the <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">31</strong><select data-qnum="31" name="question_31" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 31 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. military innovation">A. military innovation</option><option value="B. large reward">B. large reward</option><option value="C. widespread conspiracy">C. widespread conspiracy</option><option value="D. relative safety">D. relative safety</option><option value="E. new government">E. new government</option><option value="F. decisive victory">F. decisive victory</option><option value="G. political debate">G. political debate</option><option value="H. strategic alliance">H. strategic alliance</option><option value="I. popular solution">I. popular solution</option><option value="J. religious conviction">J. religious conviction</option></select></span></span> of continental Europe.</p>
</div>                                                <div class="options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--inline" data-dnd-group="7988">
                                                    <p class="dnd-panel-instruction">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</p>
                                                    <div class="dnd-cards-container">
                                                                                                                    <div class="dnd-card" draggable="true" data-value="A" data-text="A. military innovation">
                                                                <span class="dnd-label">A.</span>
                                                                <span class="dnd-text">military innovation</span>
                                                            </div>
                                                                                                                    <div class="dnd-card" draggable="true" data-value="B" data-text="B. large reward">
                                                                <span class="dnd-label">B.</span>
                                                                <span class="dnd-text">large reward</span>
                                                            </div>
                                                                                                                    <div class="dnd-card" draggable="true" data-value="C" data-text="C. widespread conspiracy">
                                                                <span class="dnd-label">C.</span>
